  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the region $\\mathrm{R}=\\left\\{(x, y):|x| \\leq|y|\\right.$ and $x^{2}$ $\\left.+y^{2} \\leq 1\\right\\}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "6b8AM",
      "text": "$\\frac{3 \\pi}{8}$ sq units",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0UZOh",
      "text": "$\\frac{5 \\pi}{8} \\mathrm{sq}$ units",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cl8xq",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ sq units",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "Jjeiz",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\pi}{8}$ sq unit",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/5nCmf5KCGMlyNK8_pS9tpwndw7e6OZXR_vf-JKknoYU.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nRequired area $=4$ (Area of the shaded region in first quadrant)\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n=4 \\int_{0}^{1 \\sqrt{2}}\\left(y_{1}-y_{2}\\right) d x=4 \\int_{0}^{1 \\sqrt{2}}\\left(\\sqrt{1-x^{2}}-x\\right) d x\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n$=4\\left[\\frac{x}{2} \\sqrt{1-x^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2} \\sin ^{-1} x-\\frac{x^{2}}{2}\\right]_{0}^{1 / \\sqrt{2}}$\r\n\r\n$=4\\left[\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{2}} \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}+\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{\\pi}{4}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right]$\r\n\r\n$=4\\left[\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{\\pi}{8}-\\frac{1}{4}\\right]=\\frac{4 \\pi}{8}=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ sq units",
    "image": null
  },
